Build and run
-------------

Requires GNU Make, a C17 compiler, and the platform's graphics libraries.
otempl downloads the raylib 6.2 release archive for the host platform into
vendor/ when creating the project (Linux amd64/arm64 or macOS).

  make
  make run
  make debug
  make release
  make clean
  make install

The Makefile links vendor/raylib-*/lib/libraylib.a and uses the headers in
that folder's include/ directory. No system raylib installation or build-time
download is required. Keep one raylib release in vendor/, or select one with:

  make RAYLIB_DIR=vendor/raylib-6.2_linux_amd64

Installation defaults to ~/.local/bin; override PREFIX (and optionally
DESTDIR) to change it.

On macOS install Xcode command-line tools. Linux requires OpenGL and X11
development libraries, plus the platform runtime dependencies. See:
https://github.com/raysan5/raylib/wiki/Working-on-GNU-Linux

Building also generates compile_flags.txt for clangd, including the selected
vendored header path. Run make once before using clangd.

The application uses a unity build: main.c includes the helper .c files and is
the only application source compiled. Add new implementation files with
#include "your_file.c" in main.c. All included files share one translation
unit, so file-scope names (including static functions and variables) must be
unique across the application.

